--TEST--
A recognized attribute's payload is checked against that attribute's own option roster rather than against a shape, so an option the roster does not name, one carrying the wrong type and one given twice are each refused at the field they are written in (`rule:core-classes/derive-attribute`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:attributes/the-names-the-compiler-acts-on
// `rule:core-classes/derive-attribute`: the compiler acts on an attribute whose name resolves to
// one of its closed `Core`-owned list, and checks that attribute's payload
// against the option roster the recognizing pass keeps for it rather than
// against a shape. The accepted row is written first, so a roster that stopped
// accepting its own two options fails here instead of as a missing refusal.
// The three after it are the three ways a payload is wrong, and each is
// reported at the field it is written in rather than at the attribute.
class Jobs {
    #[Core\Command(name: "import", about: "Read rows from a file")]
    public static function accepted(): void {}

    // An option the roster does not name. A userland attribute's literal is
    // checked under width subtyping, where this same field is accepted.
    #[Core\Command(name: "export", about: "Write rows", colour: "red")]
    public static function unknown(): void {}

    // An option carrying the wrong type.
    #[Core\Command(name: 7, about: "Count rows")]
    public static function mistyped(): void {}

    // An option given twice, which is the one a longest-match reading of the
    // payload would silently take the last of.
    #[Core\Command(name: "purge", name: "sweep", about: "Delete rows")]
    public static function twice(): void {}
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0454]: `colour` is not an option of `#[Command]`
   --> case.nvs:16:57
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `int`
   --> case.nvs:20:26
%A
error[E0304]: the option `name` is given twice
   --> case.nvs:25:35
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
